WEBVTT

symptom_01
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.161
An electronic credit note appears as
Invoice. Read the original XML. A type

symptom_02
00:00:05.161 --> 00:00:08.033
code of 381 identifies a credit note.

codes_01
00:00:08.783 --> 00:00:17.014
FACTURX and ZUGFeRD defaults also
recognize 261. Codes 383 and 384 mean

codes_02
00:00:17.014 --> 00:00:21.767
debit note and corrected invoice. Do not
classify them as credit notes.

source_01
00:00:22.517 --> 00:00:28.287
Open E-Doc for the detected format. A
custom organization transformation takes

source_02
00:00:28.287 --> 00:00:32.400
precedence over the default. Check the
active version.

transform_01
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:38.885
For FACTURX, search for INVOICE_TYPE. A
constant Invoice can discard the original

transform_02
00:00:38.885 --> 00:00:43.433
credit note code. Compare the custom
transformation with the default.

paths_01
00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:50.336
Test the transformed XML. Check that
Extraction Paths reads invoice_type from

paths_02
00:00:50.336 --> 00:00:55.067
the correct node for this format. Review
later scripts and the stored value.

activate_01
00:00:55.817 --> 00:01:01.436
Create a draft. Save does not activate it.
Test representative invoices and credit

activate_02
00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:06.000
notes. Activate with the checkmark only
after the checks pass.

safety_01
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.638
Verify a new document, including amounts
and export. Preserve custom mappings.

safety_02
00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:17.067
Before restarting an old document, check
approvals, exports and manual edits.

sign_01
00:01:17.817 --> 00:01:22.542
The negative-sign setting is enabled by
default but can be disabled. Confirm

sign_02
00:01:22.542 --> 00:01:27.867
classification and the sign convention
expected by Infor ERP or SAP.

